## Findings

1. blocking — brief:45 — Header wrapping is restricted to phone viewports. At 1280px, opening the 540px drawer beside the 220px sidebar leaves a 520px Board pane, with 472px inside its gutters. The prototype’s unwrapped title, project control, explanation and non-shrinking refresh label exceed that space; the drawer covers the overflowing refresh information. The served row checks header geometry before opening the drawer and checks the timestamp after closing it, missing this regression. — replace with: Allow the existing header to wrap whenever its available pane width requires it, including beside the open drawer at 1280px. Keep connection status and the complete last-successful-refresh time readable in live and stale states, without overlap or horizontal overflow; retain the 390px wrapping and single inset colophon. — check: `apps/web/src/components/w025.css:1076`, `apps/web/src/components/w025.css:1089`, `apps/web/src/components/w025.css:1136`, `apps/web/tests-serve/w406.spec.ts:63`

## Recommendation

